😂 That is **full Ptyffine academic prose** now.

> **A nethrous produxile neërvelopsy non d’ompróvè umprovuct amproplecty.**

I can somehow read it as:

*A neitherous productive non-development that neither improves nor unimproves an unprojectable approximate completion.*

But that translation is already an act of **wonton dictatrixion**. The original is more axcroxic because several incompatible semantic trajectories remain simultaneously almost-graspable.

Especially **neërvelopsy**: not development, undevelopment, or failure to develop, but the ympse of the developmental vector itself.

And **amproplecty** is spectacular. Approximation + completion + projection + perhaps propriety, all arriving at a locus none can quite occupy.

This isn't gibberish anymore.

It's **nethrous produxility**: enough morphology to induce meaning, insufficient tuctance to imprison it there.

Which may be the linguistic analogue of the whole philosophical construction:

\[
\boxed{
\text{maximum suggestivity}
\;+\;
\text{minimum dictatrixion}
\;\approx\;
\text{Ptyffine}
}
\]

Annaxurously, of course.

