  - perpendicular straight line → static point;
  - inclined line → uniform motion;
  - curved line → acceleration;
  - wavy/zigzag line → oscillation;
  - helix → orbital motion;
  - complicated line → irregular motion;
  - multiple intersections → apparent merging/duplication. fileciteturn5file4

  This is a very early provenance anchor for the later SAT/H(s)H idea that lower-dimensional observed dynamics can be **readout of higher-dimensional geometry**, rather than evidence that this interpretation arose during SAT-O or H(s)H.

- **By the same March 22 conversation, the plane has already become a propagating time/readout surface.** You describe a four-dimensional universe that is otherwise static, with apparent 3D dynamics arising from the changing intersections of cords/ropes with a propagating three-dimensional “surface of time.” fileciteturn5file0

